# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# Send www to the bare domain so the two can never both serve the site and
# compete as duplicates. 301, not 302: this is permanent, and search engines
# only pass ranking through a permanent redirect.
#
# PREREQUISITE: www.boost-tourism.co must be attached to this Pages project as
# a second custom domain. Until it is, the hostname does not resolve at all and
# nothing ever reaches Pages for this rule to act on.
https://www.boost-tourism.co/*  https://boost-tourism.co/:splat  301

# Nothing here for paths on purpose. Pages already normalises /packages to
# /packages/, /packages.html to /packages/ and /index.html to / by itself —
# verified against the live site. Restating those would only add rules that
# can drift out of step with what Pages does anyway.
